    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under realistic conditions. It is designed to catch silent failures \u2014 the most dangerous class of bugs in distributed systems, where a node drops out or misbehaves but the system continues returning plausible-looking output.\n\n**Core principle:** Every check must produce a *deterministic pass/fail signal*, not a subjective impression. If a check cannot be automated, define the human judgment criteria explicitly before running.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal:** Prove that every node in the cluster is running the exact same logical system.\n\n### 1.1 Model artifact identity\n- [ ] Compute a content hash (SHA-256) of the model weights on **every node** and verify all hashes match. Do not rely on file paths or filenames \u2014 files with identical names can differ in content.\n- [ ] Verify tokenizer files (vocab, merges, special tokens) hash identically across nodes.\n- [ ] Record the model revision/commit ID if loading from a registry, and confirm all nodes resolved to the same revision (a floating `latest` tag is a common source of divergence).\n- [ ] If weights are sharded across nodes (tensor/pipeline parallelism), verify shard completeness: every expected shard is present, loadable, and its hash matches the manifest.\n- [ ] Confirm quantization settings (if any) are identical: quantization method, bit width, group size, calibration data hash.\n\n### 1.2 Runtime and dependency identity\n- [ ] Record and compare versions across all nodes: inference engine, CUDA/ROCm version, driver version, NCCL/HCCL version, Python version, and key library versions.\n- [ ] Verify identical serving configuration: context length, max batch size, KV-cache size,",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
